{"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/worldmodule\/disablingentitiesandusingprefabs"]}],"abstract":[{"text":"Take entities out of play without despawning them, and spawn copies of entities and templates.","type":"text"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","text":"Overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A game often keeps entities that shouldn’t take part in a step: an enemy waiting off screen, or","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the template every goblin is copied from. A world hides those entities from queries and updates","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"while keeping their components, and it can copy any entity into a new one.","type":"text"}]},{"anchor":"Disable-an-Entity","type":"heading","text":"Disable an Entity","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Insert ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Disabled","type":"reference"},{"text":" into an entity to hide it from queries and updates. The entity stays live and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"keeps its components, and reading it through its handle still works. A query or update reaches it","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"only when it reads or writes ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Disabled"},{"text":", names it in a filter, or allows it with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".allowing(Disabled.self)"},{"text":". Remove the mark to bring the entity back.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"To make your own component types hide entities the same way, register them with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World\/registerDisablingComponent(_:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Disabling hides an entity from queries and updates only. The world’s "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World\/count"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World\/entities"},{"type":"text","text":" and the spans of "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World\/withSpan(of:_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" still include it."}]},{"anchor":"Clone-an-Entity","type":"heading","text":"Clone an Entity","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World\/clone(_:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" spawns a new entity holding a copy of every component of another. The copies"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"are new components, so they count as added and fire add and insert hooks. A clone keeps the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"original’s relations, so a clone of a child is its sibling, but the original’s children aren’t"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"cloned."}]},{"anchor":"Spawn-from-a-Prefab","type":"heading","text":"Spawn from a Prefab","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"prefab","type":"text"}]},{"text":" is an entity marked with ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Prefab","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" that holds a ready-made set of components. Queries","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and updates skip it, as they skip disabled entities, so the template never moves or takes damage","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"along with its copies. ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World\/spawn(from:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" copies a prefab without its mark, so the new entity","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"takes part like any other.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Commands"},{"text":" record clones and spawns from prefabs too, so a system can spawn copies during a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"step. The following example spawns two goblins from a prefab through commands:","type":"text"}]},{"code":["var world = World()","let goblin = world.spawn(Prefab(), Name(value: \"goblin\"), Health(current: 10))","","var commands = Commands()","commands.spawn(from: goblin)","commands.spawn(from: goblin)","world.apply(commands)","","print(world.query(Name.self).count)","\/\/ Prints \"2\"","print(world.count)","\/\/ Prints \"3\""],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"To keep a prefab outside any world, such as in a file, save it as a ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Scene","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" and spawn its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"entities into a world with ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"spawn(contentsOf:)"},{"text":"; see ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/SavingAndLoadingWorlds","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}]}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/DisablingEntitiesAndUsingPrefabs","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"kind":"article","metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"WorldModule"}],"roleHeading":"Article","title":"Disabling Entities and Using Prefabs","role":"article"},"hi